{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs63Yr86QYHWGsJkbybb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018JCuvrGpHvygcnUchtZfY9","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/alustosa/git/model-routing-eval/.work/agent-eval/2026-10-09-claude-sonnet-5-5-effort-low-r1/cases/t14_dep_resolver/resolver/SPEC.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11809,"cache_read_input_tokens":10397,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11809},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ec4aab6e-a4c4-408b-a358-152b96561758","uuid":"609224b6-8e6c-42e2-93eb-56ef0e554d83","timestamp":"2026-10-09T17:51:18.702Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs63YSpBqm7HnYoKSGuB","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_018JCuvrGpHvygcnUchtZfY9":{"file_path":"/home/alustosa/git/model-routing-eval/.work/agent-eval/2026-10-09-claude-sonnet-5-5-effort-low-r1/cases/t14_dep_resolver/resolver/SPEC.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018JCuvrGpHvygcnUchtZfY9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Resolver spec\n2\t\n3\tIndex: `dict[str, dict[str, list[str]]]`, mapping package name to a mapping of version\n4\tstring to its list of requirement strings. Example:\n5\t\n6\t```python\n7\tINDEX = {\n8\t  \"app\":  {\"1.0\": [\"web>=2\", \"db\"]},\n9\t  \"web\":  {\"1.0\": [], \"2.0\": [\"json<3\"], \"2.1\": [\"json>=3\"]},\n10\t  \"json\": {\"2.0\": [], \"3.0\": []},\n11\t  \"db\":   {\"1.0\": [\"json<3\"]},\n12\t}\n13\t```\n14\t\n15\tRequirement string grammar: `name` optionally followed by a comma-separated list of\n16\tconstraints, each `<op><version>` with op in `==`, `!=`, `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`.\n17\tExamples: `web`, `web>=2`, `json>=2,<3`, `db==1.0`.\n18\t\n19\tVersions: dotted integers, compared numerically component-wise, missing components are\n20\tzero (`1.0 == 1`, `1.10 > 1.9`).\n21\t\n22\t`resolve(roots: list[str], index) -> dict[str, str]` returns the chosen version for every\n23\tpackage in the transitive closure, such that:\n24\t\n25\t- every root requirement and every requirement of every chosen version is satisfied by the\n26\t  chosen version of that package (one version per package);\n27\t- preference: among all valid solutions, pick the one that is lexicographically greatest\n28\t  when packages are ordered by name and compared by version (i.e. the first package in\n29\t  alphabetical order gets the highest version it can, then the next, and so on);\n30\t- packages not reachable from the roots are not in the result;\n31\t- cycles in dependencies are fine (`a -> b -> a`);\n32\t- if no solution exists raise `ResolutionError` whose message names the package whose\n33\t  constraints could not be satisfied (the leaf where the search dead-ended, for example\n34\t  `b` when `a` requires `b<1` and only `b 1` and `b 2` exist), not only the root.\n35\t\n36\tCorrectness over speed, but the hidden tests include an index with a few hundred\n37\tversions where naive full enumeration will time out (60 s). Backtracking with\n38\tconstraint propagation is enough.\n39\t\n40\tAlso export `Version` (comparable, hashable, `str()` gives the original string) and\n41\t`Constraint.parse(\"json>=2,<3\")` with `.name` and `.allows(Version)`.\n42\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ec4aab6e-a4c4-408b-a358-152b96561758","uuid":"0e010845-35f7-4ed1-95c4-fc62814cf13d","timestamp":"2026-10-09T17:51:18.768Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/alustosa/git/model-routing-eval/.work/agent-eval/2026-10-09-claude-sonnet-5-5-effort-low-r1/cases/t14_dep_resolver/resolver/SPEC.md","content":"# Resolver spec\n\nIndex: `dict[str, dict[str, list[str]]]`, mapping package name to a mapping of version\nstring to its list of requirement strings. Example:\n\n```python\nINDEX = {\n  \"app\":  {\"1.0\": [\"web>=2\", \"db\"]},\n  \"web\":  {\"1.0\": [], \"2.0\": [\"json<3\"], \"2.1\": [\"json>=3\"]},\n  \"json\": {\"2.0\": [], \"3.0\": []},\n  \"db\":   {\"1.0\": [\"json<3\"]},\n}\n```\n\nRequirement string grammar: `name` optionally followed by a comma-separated list of\nconstraints, each `<op><version>` with op in `==`, `!=`, `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`.\nExamples: `web`, `web>=2`, `json>=2,<3`, `db==1.0`.\n\nVersions: dotted integers, compared numerically component-wise, missing components are\nzero (`1.0 == 1`, `1.10 > 1.9`).\n\n`resolve(roots: list[str], index) -> dict[str, str]` returns the chosen version for every\npackage in the transitive closure, such that:\n\n- every root requirement and every requirement of every chosen version is satisfied by the\n  chosen version of that package (one version per package);\n- preference: among all valid solutions, pick the one that is lexicographically greatest\n  when packages are ordered by name and compared by version (i.e. the first package in\n  alphabetical order gets the highest version it can, then the next, and so on);\n- packages not reachable from the roots are not in the result;\n- cycles in dependencies are fine (`a -> b -> a`);\n- if no solution exists raise `ResolutionError` whose message names the package whose\n  constraints could not be satisfied (the leaf where the search dead-ended, for example\n  `b` when `a` requires `b<1` and only `b 1` and `b 2` exist), not only the root.\n\nCorrectness over speed, but the hidden tests include an index with a few hundred\nversions where naive full enumeration will time out (60 s). Backtracking with\nconstraint propagation is enough.\n\nAlso export `Version` (comparable, hashable, `str()` gives the original string) and\n`Constraint.parse(\"json>=2,<3\")` with `.name` and `.allows(Version)`.\n","numLines":42,"startLine":1,"totalLines":42}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018JCuvrGpHvygcnUchtZfY9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
